    "id": "p10-q17",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "For what value of $n$ is $\\dfrac{nx-6}{x-2}=3$ true for all $x\\ne2$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=3$.",
      "worked": "The numerator must equal $3(x-2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}nx-6&=3(x-2)\\\\nx-6&=3x-6\\end{align*}$$\nComparing the coefficients of $x$ gives $n=3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
